# Citation metadata for the GLACE dataset, read by GitHub (docs/DESIGN.md §7). `version`
# is one string with DATASET_VERSION and the two collection documents;
# tests/test_version.py enforces that. `date-released` is written in the release commit itself.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: Use the version-specific DOI to cite the exact dataset version used.
type: dataset
title: GLACE Alps
abstract: >-
  Annual summer composites of Sentinel-1 12-day repeat-pass interferometric
  coherence (COH12) and radiometrically terrain-corrected backscatter (RTC) for
  the Alpine Convention perimeter, 2015–2026. Each composite covers a 90-day
  summer window and weights the observations by their local resolution. The
  data is distributed as single tiles (MGRS grid, 10 m) per year and grid cell
  and as mosaics (ETRS89-LAEA, 20 m) per year.
authors:
  - family-names: Gentner
    given-names: Luis Q.
    email: luis.gentner@geo.uzh.ch
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4453-0881
    affiliation: University of Zurich, Department of Geography
  - family-names: Piermattei
    given-names: Livia
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2814-8659
    affiliation: University of Zurich, Department of Geography
  - family-names: Wulf
    given-names: Hendrik
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6161-428X
    affiliation: University of Zurich, Department of Geography
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: https://github.com/lqgentner/glace-catalog
url: https://source.coop/giuz/glace-alps
# The DOI of this version, bumped with it; tests/test_version.py checks it
# against metadata/catalog.yaml. The canonical DOI names every version.
doi: 10.48656/60er-3j55
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.48656/d4r9-fj97
    description: Canonical DOI, every version
version: "1.0"
keywords:
  - Sentinel-1
  - SAR
  - InSAR coherence
  - backscatter
  - glaciers
  - cryosphere
  - Alps
  - STAC
